CodeBrix patch 0005 - zero-initialized workgroup memory by default (wgpu-native/src/lib.rs)

WHAT: the compute stage and the vertex / fragment stages of the pipeline conversions pass
zero_initialize_workgroup_memory: true (it was hard-coded false, marked "TODO(wgpu.h)").
WHY: WebGPU requires workgroup (var<workgroup>) memory to start zeroed, and Rust wgpu's default is
true; with false a shader that reads shared memory before writing it reads whatever the driver left
there. No option is added: wgpu.h has no pipeline-descriptor extras struct to carry one, and adding
one would change the C API; true is the safe default.
UPSTREAM: trunk (589e6caa4e) still hard-codes false. Open PR #630 adds
WGPUComputePipelineDescriptorExtras.zeroInitializeWorkgroupMemory (a wgpu 30-era header change)
but still defaults to false without the extras. CodeBrix's own change.

--- a/wgpu-native/src/lib.rs
+++ b/wgpu-native/src/lib.rs
@@ -2158,7 +2158,9 @@ pub unsafe extern "C" fn wgpuDeviceCreateComputePipeline(
             })
             .collect(),
             // TODO(wgpu.h)
-            zero_initialize_workgroup_memory: false,
+            // CodeBrix (patches/0005): WebGPU requires workgroup memory to start zeroed (Rust
+            // wgpu's default is true too); `false` let shaders read stale shared memory.
+            zero_initialize_workgroup_memory: true,
         },
         // TODO(wgpu.h)
         cache: None,
